  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_hedlake_cb0">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>linen cloth made of Werg (the unworked stem or fiber of flax, before it is heckled; the fiber of flax, hemp or jute prepared for spinning by some process of scutching; the shorter fibers of flax which are separated by heckling from the fine and long-stapled (OED s.v. tow n.^1 1, 2a)) (Pitz 550) | linen cloth made of Werg (refuse flax) (Pitz 550) | linen cloth made of Werg (the unworked stem or fiber of flax, before it is heckled; the fiber of flax, hemp or jute prepared for spinning by some process of scutching; the shorter fibers of flax which are separated by heckling from the fine and long-stapled (OED s.v. tow n.1 1, 2a)) (Pitz 550)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
